      "statement": "The purpose of the first-class Unknown is to keep RESOLVED-UNKNOWN ('cannot yet be proven', verdict UNKNOWN) distinct from a hard fail ('proven wrong', the contradicted case), so downstream consumers can distinguish the two rather than overclaiming failures.",
