    {
      "id": "claim_bb904d719cab48eca2c07b0605d31743",
      "statement": "Verification under OWA is a three-way epistemic grading: verified (entailed by the KB), contradicted (negated by the TBox, a consistency failure), and unverified-unknown (some completions support it, some don't, carrying why-unknown and resolving evidence). The rule is to never emit 'false' merely because a fact is absent.",
